# Answer 7 · Gender Studies versus Women's Studies; the Historical Need, Scope and Significance of Gender Studies, with Reference to Pakistan (CSS 2019)
@py question 2019-2

## The answer map
::: fig mindmap | The answer map: every branch is one numbered heading of the model answer below.
@note Four tasks: differentiate; trace the need in dated phases; scope and significance; bring Pakistan into every part.
@ask ① DIFFERENTIATE GS from WS
@ask ② TRACE historically the need for GS as a distinct discipline
@ask ③ its SCOPE and SIGNIFICANCE — with special reference to PAKISTAN
(1) Introduction: WS puts women at the centre; GS studies gender relations; each phase exposed a gap
(2) The difference: table of six points; WS is women, GS is relations and power
(3) Phase 1, before 1960s: knowledge treated men as the norm; women missing
(4) Phase 2, 1969–70s: the women's movement created Women's Studies
(5) Phase 3, 1980s–90s: gender idea, men's studies, queer theory, intersectionality
(6) Phase 4, 1985–95: aid agencies and Beijing needed gender experts
(7) Scope: family, work, politics, culture, violence, climate
(8) Significance: complete knowledge; policy tools; words for hidden harms
